"""Narration source: continuous spoken prose, with separate animation cue times.

Each tuple begins a visual beat; scenes hold on it with ``beat(scene, t, i)``.
Export joins the prose for a voice recording or TTS and writes cue sheets
separately; cue times are editorial targets, not TTS pauses.

Every number, count and verdict spoken here is checked against the models
by ``python -m utils.mo_data`` — change a filling or a value there and the
check names the line that no longer agrees.

Spelling for the cloned voice: numbers are written out; orbital labels are
written "sigma two p", "pi star"; formulas are written "O two plus",
"H two". LCAO is spelled out letter by letter ("L C A O").
"""

