        (19.5, "Hund's rule again: one in each, spins parallel. They occupy different bonding pi orbitals."),
        (25.5, "Bond order one, and two unpaired electrons. B two is paramagnetic, which a simple Lewis structure doesn't suggest."),
        (35.0, "Fluorine. Seven each, fourteen in total. Oxygen's ordering. This time the bonding sigma lies below pi."),
        (41.5, "Fill everything oxygen had, then two more. Pi star fills completely. Those last two electrons enter antibonding states."),
        (48.5, "Eight bonding, six antibonding. Bond order one. Every spin paired. Diamagnetic. The outer electrons leave just one net bond."),
        (56.0, "Line them up. Boron, one. Nitrogen, three. Oxygen, two. Fluorine, one. Equal bond order need not mean equal magnetism."),
